            <ArticleTitle>Aristolochic acid derivatives from the rhizome of Arisolochia championii.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>63-68</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0367-326X(16)31022-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fitote.2017.01.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Four new aristolochic acid derivatives aristchamic A (1), aristchamic B (2), aristochamic C (3a), aristchamic D (3b) and one new aristolactam aristolactam-CV (4), together with 10 known compounds (5-14), were isolated from the rhizomes of Aristolochia championii. Their structures were assigned by detailed analysis of MS and NMR spectroscopic data. All of the isolated compounds were evaluated for their cytotoxic activities against HCT-116, HepG2, BGC-823, NCI-H1650, and A2780 cell. Compound 1 exhibited significant cytotoxic activity against HCT-116, HepG2, BGC-823, and NCI-H1650, with IC50 values of 0.50, 7.37, 2.66, and 0.75μM, respectively.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier B.V.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
